Z||000000||stsmithgt||11-21-2000||09:50 AM||||I thought the title would get your attention.  I hope it doesn't rain today because our company got some tickets to go  to Laguna Seca to ride in Ferraris.  I was lucky enough to be maxed out with vacation time to bargain with to get a ticket from them. Unfortunately it will be driven by a professional driver instead of me. We'll be taking hot laps around the track.  I had to mention this.  I've always wanted to take my GT out on the track, but I guess this is the closest at this time I'm going to get(so far).  This is going to be COOOOOOOOOOl. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I hope they let me take my camera in the car. pics pics pics.||||reg||14
Z||000001||bHooper||11-21-2000||11:20 AM||||you are going to love that!  Laguna Seca is a beautifull track.<P>in september I had the oportunity to take touring laps in my GT around Virginia International Raceway (a very nice, rebuilt old roadcourse)... man that was a blast!<P>i cant wait to go back around it next spring, with my rebuilt suspension and brakes!<P>enjoy! and remember not to drool to much, Ferrari owners don't like that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/alien.gif">   <BR>We are not alone!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Coconut||11-21-2000||01:40 PM||||Now that would be WAY cool! While you're at it, see if this driver can duplicate Alex Zanardi's move on Bryan Herta thru the corkscrew back in '96! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> THE gutsiest move I have ever seen! Have a blast dude! I wish I was in your shoes!<P>Cruisin' On, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||14
