Z||000004||dodger||11-21-2000||11:20 PM||||Wow...Just thought I'd tell you...I work over by Laureles Grade and can hear the laps at Laguna Seca from work. <BR>Dodger Red '86 2M6<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||11-22-2000||10:03 AM||||WOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO! THAT WAS A BLAST!<BR>It was dry the first half of the day so they were ripping around the track.  That first lap was intense!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  We got up to around 140 down the front straight.  I thought 80 was pretty fast diving into the hairpin at the end.  The "G" forces felt great!  I got to ride in a couple of different Ferraris.  The handling and breaking was awesome.  The second half of the day it did sprinkle, but Terry, rain or shine they kept driving!  a few of the cars spun out on turn 11 just before the front straight.  There's plenty of room for error there.  I'm going to have to do that again sometime.  I sacraficed 6 of my laps and gave them to an old school buddy of mine.  I figured you don't get to do this sort of thing everyday so I thought I'd spread it around a little.  I'll try and bring up some pics.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00067.jpg">  this was the car I got to ride in when it was dry. Man did he rip around the track.  Actually he could of gone faster, but there was a db limit.  Couldn't get over 90db that day.  Damn snobs on the hill shouldn't be there if they don't like racing!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00057.jpg"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 11-22-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000006||ChadMan||11-22-2000||11:33 AM||||Man, am I jealous.  Before I die, I want to drive Laguna Seca at speed.<P>By the way - did you see the family of Gonzalo Rodriguez is suing Laguna Seca and CART?  What's up with that?||||reg||10
Z||000007||stsmithgt||11-22-2000||11:41 AM||||I'm not up on that suit. What is it, their poodle is traumatized by the noise?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> I'm sure there's plenty of them from all the fu#$%^ bastards that move next to the track and then start complaining.  They *****  about the airport too.  They have nothing better to do than complain with there rich old money.  Most of those people moved in AFTER the track was built.  I just saw new contruction over the hill from the track.  I only see more trouble with that.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>OH YEAH! the blue ticket is the key to the ride. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00063.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 11-22-2000).]||||reg||5
